# Nothing ROM-shaped, ever. This project ships coordinates and code, never
# cartridge bytes: supply your own dump (see "No ROM ships with this" in
# the README) and the tools will find it.
*.a78
*.bin
*.rom
*.car
*.atr
*.atx
*.xex

# .bps and .abp are the exception, and deliberately so: both exist to be
# distributed without carrying the game. Audited rather than assumed --
# across every .bps here, 18936 stored literal bytes and not one of them
# equal to the original at the same address, because the encoder only
# emits a literal for a run that differs. The .abp is stronger still: its
# sections store a CRC32 of the pre-image instead of the pre-image, and
# its float blobs are authored code that appears nowhere in the ROM.
# Re-run tools/selftest.py, which checks that guarantee, before relaxing
# anything else here.
!dist/*.bps
!dist/*.abp

# ...nor anything decoded out of one. `assets/` holds sprite sheets
# rendered straight from cartridge graphics and `snap/` holds emulator
# screenshots; both are game artwork and both regenerate from a dump.
assets/
snap/

# Emulator and session leftovers rather than source.
cfg/
*.log
*.inp
*.wav
*.lnk

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
